				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(392303); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=392303&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609016580" alt="Voct" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=392303)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/voct" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(392303); return false;" >Voct</a></span> <span class="odate time_1384001654 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Nov 2013 12:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1888982">
									

<p>&lt;Spidersnake&gt; Green farting floating skywriting sloths controlled by an angry guy in a suit. I like it, but don't be surprised when people complain about a lack of hook<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; Spidersnake - I should point out, the green part is common to real sloths<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; as is the farting<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; this guy was able to anomalously breed a population of sloths that has these capabilities whcih are not strictly anomalous<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; but, uh<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; it's the result of anomalous animal husbandry<br />
&lt;Spidersnake&gt; Well, are regular sloths smart enough to understand basic commands? I truly don't know.<br />
&lt;Bunton&gt; It wouldn't be /anomalous/ in a Foundation sense if you got one that was.<br />
&lt;Bunton&gt; Especially intelligent varieties of certain animals aren't that uncommon.<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; Bunton - but to breed an entire population of sloths that a) can float, b) can fart skywriting, and c) are instinctively obedient to white-haired men who wear suits with orange neckties and who speak English with a New York accent?<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; I really like the idea of this anomalous businessman feverishly breeding sloths in his basement, knowing that in just 450 more accelerated generations, they'll be able to fly<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; imagine a Batman villain whose gimmick is &quot;breeding anomalous sloths&quot;<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; now I'm imagiing the Foundation tracking down the Sloth Wrangler and somehow coercing him into breeding sloths that could destroy SCP-682<br />
&lt;Berggren&gt; Voct: the point is not totally in the breedin of the sloths but in the fact that they were used as retaliation for corporate espionage<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; Berggren - that may have been what the Sloth Wrangler used them for, but what the Foundation is interested in is the fact that the guy *is* the Sloth Wrangler<br />
&lt;Berggren&gt; Voct: sure<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; &quot;FUK U FUKRE&quot; - beautiful<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; Berggren - every now and then, the Sloth Wrangler gets lonely, and starts to consider how long it would take to breed a sloth that would look and act like a human female. But then he gets all angry at himself for being a pervert.<br />
&lt;Voct&gt; Still, though. It'd take him 851 days.</p>

